From a088c0436b04b4241659995bd617d12db23df195 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 02:41:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 49/56] Trainer Tower: competitive teams

Every Trainer Tower Pokemon is rebuilt as a competitive set: fully
evolved (one per species per team), moves from Showdown's role-based
random-battle sets (doubles sets on Double floors; Gen 9 first, then
older generations) limited to learnable moves, 252/252 EVs and a role
nature, perfect IVs, a matching ability and a role item with no repeats.
Generated by tools/hack/tower_sets.py.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JQmLEZftLdDmGYX3wiQ71G
---
 HACK_NOTES.md            |   21 +
 src/trainer_tower_sets.c | 9993 +++++++++++++++++++-------------------
 tools/hack/tower_sets.py |  263 +
 3 files changed, 5281 insertions(+), 4996 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 tools/hack/tower_sets.py

diff --git a/HACK_NOTES.md b/HACK_NOTES.md
index 794f253..9781e38 100644
--- a/HACK_NOTES.md
+++ b/HACK_NOTES.md
@@ -465,6 +465,25 @@ How the cap works with each way of gaining levels:
   252 in Speed (or in HP for slow Pokémon). Each peak trainer carries Full
   Restores.
 
+## Trainer Tower (Seven Island)
+Every Trainer Tower trainer now uses competitive sets, built the way real
+teams are:
+- **Fully evolved:** every Pokémon, using the later evolutions where they
+  exist (e.g. Magmortar, Togekiss, Scizor, Porygon-Z). There's one of each
+  species per team.
+- **Moves from real roles:** they come from Pokémon Showdown's role-based
+  sets (Fast Attacker, Setup Sweeper, Bulky Support and so on), limited to
+  moves in this hack that the Pokémon can learn.
+  - On Double floors, the sets come from the doubles format, with Protect,
+    spread moves, Helping Hand, Follow Me and Trick Room.
+- **EVs, nature and IVs:** 252/252 EVs and a nature that suit the role, and
+  perfect IVs.
+- **Ability and item:** a fitting ability, and a held item for the role
+  (Choice Band, Leftovers, Lum or Sitrus Berry, or a type booster), with no
+  item repeated on a team.
+
+Opponents still scale to your highest-level Pokémon, as in the original.
+
 ## True endgame (after beating the round 2 Champion)
 The Champion's rematch (round 2) unlocks once the Sevii Islands story is
 done. The first time you beat it, or the peak round 3, you get:
@@ -489,6 +508,8 @@ Each script runs once against the original pret data:
   an unused species slot, with its graphics, cry, Pokédex entry and evolution item.
 - `balance.py`: modern boss movesets, peak teams with the later evolutions.
 - `validate.py`: checks the game data for missing or inconsistent entries.
+- `tower_sets.py <dir>`: the competitive Trainer Tower teams, from Showdown's
+  random-battle set files (read as data).
 - `gym_doubles.py`: the gym double battles (one trainer per gym) and their doubles movesets.
 - `learnsets.py`: what each species can learn in this hack (used by the scripts that set trainer moves).
 - `vr_rematches.py`: the Victory Road VS Seeker rematch teams and scripts.
